# API and Environment

## Environment

Backend API base URL → `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` in `.env.local`, read via `src/lib/env.ts` (`getPublicApiBaseUrl()`). Never hardcode hosts in code.

## API paths

API path segments only → `src/lib/constants/api.ts` (`API_ENDPOINTS`).

## Data fetching

Custom data-fetching hooks → `src/hooks/use<Feature>.ts`.

## Example

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/users");

// ✅ GOOD
import { getPublicApiBaseUrl } from "@/lib/env";
import { API_ENDPOINTS } from "@/lib/constants/api";
const res = await fetch(`${getPublicApiBaseUrl()}${API_ENDPOINTS.users}`);
```
